# DevIndex DERIVED data — regenerated every run, never versioned.
#
# These three are ~26.5 MiB rewritten in full on every pipeline run. Committing them is how the same
# file in neomjs/neo reached 1,802 commits behind a 4.1 GB .git; this repository's is 14 MB and stays
# that way. `users.jsonl` arrives via `npm run devindex:pull-data` (also run from postinstall) and is
# written into the deployed build by the publish step; `tracker.json` and `visited.json` are pipeline
# state with no browser consumer at all.
#
# The CURATED files in the same directory are deliberately NOT ignored — allowlist, blocklist,
# failed, optin-sync, optout-sync, threshold, and index-provenance.json total 543 bytes and cannot be
# regenerated. `blocklist.json` carries somebody's opt-out decision. Ignoring the directory wholesale
# would discard that audit trail silently, which is why the guard asserts they stay tracked.
/apps/devindex/resources/data/users.jsonl
/apps/devindex/resources/data/tracker.json
/apps/devindex/resources/data/visited.json

